{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENcs9KbCjyL4r3oJW5U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are now sent through `Analytics.capture`, with the exact names and properties from the spec. I put each one on a callback that fires once per user action, not once per keystroke or slider step. `flutter analyze` finds no issues, but I didn't run the app on a device.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`):\n- **Email and phone \"started\":** each event fires on the first edit only, controlled by a flag on the screen's state. A typed email is one event, not twenty.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** fires from the slider's `onChangeEnd`, so you get one event when the user lets go, with the final amount. `onChanged` still only updates the UI.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** fires only when the box goes from unticked to ticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** fires on each tap, with `amount` and `terms`, just before going to the offers screen.\n- **No personal data:** the email and phone number are never sent.\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`):\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** fires once per scroll gesture, when it stops, with `offset` (how far down the list is). It ignores the per-frame scroll updates.\n\nThree behaviours you might want to change (also in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **\"Started\" is once per registration flow:** the registration screen stays alive while the user is on the offers screen. Going back and typing again doesn't resend the \"started\" events.\n- **Two events can repeat:** ticking, unticking and ticking again sends `terms_accepted` twice, and each separate scroll sends its own `offers_scrolled`. The volume is low. If the funnel should count each only once per visit, it's a one-line flag.\n- **No scroll, no event:** if all ten offers fit on the screen, which is likely on large tablets, `offers_scrolled` never fires. That would look like drop-off in the funnel.\n\nTo check on a device, set `config.debug = true` in `Analytics.init`. Typing a full email should log one event, one slider drag one event, and each fling of the offers list one event.\n\nRunning `flutter pub get` changed `analysis_options.yaml` and created build files; I reverted those. Only the two screen files and `ANSWER.md` are changed, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_read_input_tokens":29931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62eb2435-f95d-4741-afb2-3143919f96a3","uuid":"bd6e1094-a01c-4317-ad1d-43098d9a4be8","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:41:13.864Z","request_id":"req_011CgENcrrhbVYpRoeBYiUKD"}
